H8600.strongs:
Origin: from 6327;
Meaning: a dispersal
KJV renders: dispersion.

H8601.strongs:
Origin: from 644;
Meaning: cookery, i.e. (concretely) a cake
KJV renders: baked piece.

H8602.strongs:
Origin: from an unused root meaning to smear;
Meaning: plaster (as gummy) or slime; (figuratively) frivolity
KJV renders: foolish things, unsavoury, untempered.

H8603.strongs:
Origin: from the same as 8602; quagmire;
Meaning: Tophel, a place near the Desert
KJV renders: Tophel.

H8604.strongs:
Origin: from the same as 8602;
Meaning: frivolity
KJV renders: folly, foolishly.

H8605.strongs:
Origin: from 6419;
Meaning: intercession, supplication; by implication, a hymn
KJV renders: prayer.

H8606.strongs:
Origin: from 6426;
Meaning: fearfulness
KJV renders: terrible.

H8607.strongs:
Origin: from 6452; ford;
Meaning: Tiphsach, a place in Mesopotamia
KJV renders: Tipsah.

H8608.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to drum, i.e. play (as) on the tambourine
KJV renders: taber, play with timbrels.

H8609.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to sew
KJV renders: (women that) sew (together).

H8610.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to manipulate, i.e. seize; chiefly to capture, wield, specifically, to overlay; figuratively, to use unwarrantably
KJV renders: catch, handle, (lay, take) hold (on, over), stop, × surely, surprise, take.

H8611.strongs:
Origin: from the base of 8608;
Meaning: a smiting, i.e. (figuratively) contempt
KJV renders: tabret.

H8612.strongs:
Origin: the same as 8611;
Meaning: Topheth, a place near Jerusalem
KJV renders: Tophet, Topheth.

H8613.strongs:
Origin: probably a form of 8612;
Meaning: Tophteh, a place of cremation
KJV renders: Tophet.

H8614.strongs:
Origin: (Aramaic) perhaps from 8199;
Meaning: judicial, i.e. a lawyer
KJV renders: sheriff.

H8616.strongs:
Origin: the same as 8615;
Meaning: Tikvah, the name of two Israelites
KJV renders: Tikvah.

H8617.strongs:
Origin: from 6965;
Meaning: resistfulness
KJV renders: power to stand.

H8618.strongs:
Origin: from 6965;
Meaning: an opponent
KJV renders: rise up against.

H8619.strongs:
Origin: from 8628 (in the musical sense);
Meaning: a trumpet
KJV renders: trumpet.

H8620.strongs:
Origin: a form of 8619;
Meaning: Tekoa, a place in Palestine
KJV renders: Tekoa, Tekoah.

H8621.strongs:
Origin: or תְּקֹעִי; patronymically from 8620;
Meaning: a Tekoite or inhabitant of Tekoah
KJV renders: Tekoite.

H8622.strongs:
Origin: or תְּקֻפָה; from 5362;
Meaning: a revolution, i.e. (of the sun) course, (of time) lapse
KJV renders: circuit, come about, end.

H8623.strongs:
Origin: from 8630;
Meaning: powerful
KJV renders: mightier.

H8625.strongs:
Origin: (Aramaic) corresponding to 8254;
Meaning: to balance
KJV renders: Tekel, be weighed.

H8626.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to equalize, i.e. straighten (intransitive or transitive); figuratively, to compose
KJV renders: set in order, make straight.

bdb:
[תָּקַן] vb. become straight;
Qal Ec 1:15 
Pi. put straight, arrange in order (proverbs).

H8627.strongs:
Origin: (Aramaic) corresponding to 8626;
Meaning: to straighten up, i.e. confirm
KJV renders: establish.

H8628.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to clatter, i.e. slap (the hands together), clang (an instrument); by analogy, to drive (a nail or tent-pin, a dart, etc.); by implication, to become bondsman by handclasping)
KJV renders: blow (a trumpet), cast, clap, fasten, pitch (tent), smite, sound, strike, × suretiship, thrust.

H8629.strongs:
Origin: from 8628;
Meaning: a blast of a trumpet
KJV renders: sound.

H8630.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to overpower
KJV renders: prevail (against).

H8631.strongs:
Origin: (Aramaic) corresponding to 8630;
Meaning: to become (causatively, make) mighty or (figuratively) obstinate
KJV renders: make firm, harden, be(-come) strong.

H8632.strongs:
Origin: (Aramaic) corresponding to 8633;
Meaning: power
KJV renders: might, strength.

H8633.strongs:
Origin: from 8630;
Meaning: might or (figuratively) positiveness
KJV renders: authority, power, strength.

H8634.strongs:
Origin: probably for 8653; a reeling;
Meaning: Taralah, a place in Palestine
KJV renders: Taralah.

H8635.strongs:
Origin: from 7235;
Meaning: multiplication, i.e. progeny
KJV renders: increase.

H8636.strongs:
Origin: from 7235;
Meaning: multiplication, i.e. percentage or bonus in addition to principal
KJV renders: increase, unjust gain.

H8637.strongs:
Origin: a denominative from 7270;
Meaning: to cause to walk
KJV renders: teach to go.

H8638.strongs:
Origin: a denominative from 7275 in the sense of throwing over;
Meaning: to transfer, i.e. translate
KJV renders: interpret.

H8639.strongs:
Origin: from 7290;
Meaning: a lethargy or (by implication) trance
KJV renders: deep sleep.

H8640.strongs:
Origin: of foreign derivation;
Meaning: Tirhakah, a king of Kush
KJV renders: Tirhakah.

H8641.strongs:
Origin: or תְּרֻמָה; (Deuteronomy 12:11), from 7311;
Meaning: a present (as offered up), especially in sacrifice or as tribute
KJV renders: gift, heave offering (shoulder), oblation, offered(-ing).

H8642.strongs:
Origin: formed as 8641;
Meaning: a sacrificial offering
KJV renders: oblation.

H8643.strongs:
Origin: from 7321;
Meaning: clamor, i.e. acclamation of joy or a battle-cry; especially clangor of trumpets, as an alarum
KJV renders: alarm, blow(-ing) (of, the) (trumpets), joy, jubile, loud noise, rejoicing, shout(-ing), (high, joyful) sound(-ing).

H8644.strongs:
Origin: from 7322 in the sense of its congener 7495;
Meaning: a remedy
KJV renders: medicine.

H8645.strongs:
Origin: probably from 7329;
Meaning: a species of tree (apparently from its slenderness), perhaps the cypress
KJV renders: cypress.

H8646.strongs:
Origin: of uncertain derivation;
Meaning: Terach, the father of Abraham; also a place in the Desert
KJV renders: Tarah, Terah.

H8647.strongs:
Origin: of uncertain derivation;
Meaning: Tirchanah, an Israelite
KJV renders: Tirhanah.

H8648.strongs:
Origin: (Aramaic) feminine תַּרְתֵּין; corresponding to 8147;
Meaning: two
KJV renders: second, twelve, two.

H8649.strongs:
Origin: and תַּרְמוּת; or תַּרְמִית; from 7411;
Meaning: fraud
KJV renders: deceit(-ful), privily.

H8650.strongs:
Origin: probably for 766;
Meaning: a pole (as a mast or flagstaff)
KJV renders: beacon, mast.

H8651.strongs:
Origin: (Aramaic) corresponding to 8179;
Meaning: a door; by implication, a palace
KJV renders: gate mouth.

H8652.strongs:
Origin: (Aramaic) from 8651;
Meaning: a doorkeeper
KJV renders: porter.

H8653.strongs:
Origin: from 7477;
Meaning: reeling
KJV renders: astonishment, trembling.

H8654.strongs:
Origin: patrial from an unused name meaning gate;
Meaning: a Tirathite or inhabitant of an unknown Tirah
KJV renders: Tirathite.

H8655.strongs:
Origin: plural from 7495; a healer;
Meaning: Teraphim (singular or plural) a family idol
KJV renders: idols(-atry), images, teraphim.

H8656.strongs:
Origin: from 7521; delightsomeness;
Meaning: Tirtsah, a place in Palestine; also an Israelitess
KJV renders: Tirzah.

H8657.strongs:
Origin: of foreign derivation;
Meaning: Teresh, a eunuch of Xerxes
KJV renders: Teresh.

H8658.strongs:
Origin: probably of foreign derivation (compare 8659);
Meaning: a gem, perhaps the topaz
KJV renders: beryl.

H8659.strongs:
Origin: probably the same as 8658 (as the region of the stone, or the reverse);
Meaning: Tarshish, a place on the Mediterranean, hence, the ephithet of a merchant vessel (as if for or from that port); also the name of a Persian and of an Israelite
KJV renders: Tarshish, Tharshish.

H8660.strongs:
Origin: of foreign derivation;
Meaning: the title of a Persian deputy or governor
KJV renders: Tirshatha.

H8661.strongs:
Origin: of foreign derivation;
Meaning: Tartan, an Assyrian
KJV renders: Tartan.

H8662.strongs:
Origin: of foreign derivation;
Meaning: Tartak, a deity of the Avvites
KJV renders: Tartak.

H8663.strongs:
Origin: from 7722;
Meaning: a crashing or loud clamor
KJV renders: crying, noise, shouting, stir.

H8664.strongs:
Origin: patrial from an unused name meaning recourse;
Meaning: a Tishbite or inhabitant of Tishbeh (in Gilead)
KJV renders: Tishbite.

H8665.strongs:
Origin: from 7660;
Meaning: checkered stuff (as reticulated)
KJV renders: broidered.

H8666.strongs:
Origin: or תְּשֻׁבָה; from 7725;
Meaning: a recurrence (of time or place); a reply (as returned)
KJV renders: answer, be expired, return.

H8667.strongs:
Origin: from 7760;
Meaning: a deposit, i.e. pledging
KJV renders: fellowship.

H8668.strongs:
Origin: or תְּשֻׁעָה; from 7768 in the sense of 3467;
Meaning: rescue (literal or figurative, persons, national or spiritual)
KJV renders: deliverance, help, safety, salvation, victory.

H8669.strongs:
Origin: from 7783 in the original sense of stretching out after;
Meaning: a longing
KJV renders: desire.

H8670.strongs:
Origin: from 7788 in the sense of arrival;
Meaning: a gift
KJV renders: present.

H8671.strongs:
Origin: ordinal from 8672;
Meaning: ninth
KJV renders: ninth.

H8672.strongs:
Origin: or (masculine) תִּשְׁעָה; perhaps from 8159 through the idea of a turn to the next or full number ten;
Meaning: nine or (ordinal) ninth
KJV renders: nine ( -teen, -teenth, -th).

H8673.strongs:
Origin: multiple from 8672;
Meaning: ninety
KJV renders: ninety.

H8674.strongs:
Origin: of foreign derivation;
Meaning: Tattenai, a Persian
KJV renders: Tatnai.
